---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { S, UPDATED, SOURCE_URL, CFR_URL, NHTSA_GUIDE } from '../../lib/data';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Data', href: '/data/' }];
const origin = Astro.site!.origin;
const files = [
  ['nhtsa-utqg-records.csv', 'text/csv', 'Normalized record-level table (one row per NHTSA record)'],
  ['nhtsa-utqg-records.json', 'application/json', 'Same as CSV, JSON'],
  ['nhtsa-utqg-lines.json', 'application/json', 'One object per tire line with computed median, percentile and brand rank'],
  ['nhtsa-utqg-sizes.json', 'application/json', 'Per-size rows of lines with an explicit size record'],
  ['summary.json', 'application/json', 'Counts and pull metadata'],
];
const ld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Dataset', name: 'NHTSA UTQG tire ratings, normalized', description: `Normalized copy of ${S.raw_records} NHTSA Uniform Tire Quality Grading records (treadwear, traction, temperature) with parsed tire sizes and computed line statistics.`, url: new URL('/data/', origin).href, dateModified: UPDATED, creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (source data)' }, isBasedOn: SOURCE_URL, license: 'https://www.usa.gov/government-works', isAccessibleForFree: true, version: UPDATED, keywords: ['tire treadwear', 'UTQG', 'uniform tire quality grading', 'tire traction grade', 'tire temperature grade', 'NHTSA'], spatialCoverage: 'United States', temporalCoverage: UPDATED, measurementTechnique: 'Grades are assigned by tire makers under 49 CFR 575.104 and published by NHTSA; this copy normalizes brand, line and size text.', citation: 'https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/subtitle-B/chapter-V/part-575/subpart-B/section-575.104', publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'TireMileage', url: new URL('/', origin).href }, variableMeasured: [{ '@type': 'PropertyValue', name: 'treadwear', description: 'UTQG treadwear grade, relative wear rate vs. control tire graded 100' }, { '@type': 'PropertyValue', name: 'traction', description: 'UTQG traction grade AA, A, B or C (wet braking)' }, { '@type': 'PropertyValue', name: 'temperature', description: 'UTQG temperature grade A, B or C (heat resistance)' }], distribution: files.map(([f, t]) => ({ '@type': 'DataDownload', encodingFormat: t, contentUrl: new URL(`/data/${f}`, origin).href })) }];
---
<Base title="Download the NHTSA UTQG Tire Ratings Dataset (CSV, JSON)" description={`Free normalized CSV/JSON of ${S.raw_records.toLocaleString()} NHTSA tire treadwear, traction and temperature records with parsed sizes.`} crumbs={crumbs} ld={ld}>
  <h1>Dataset downloads</h1>
  <div class="answer">The full normalized dataset ({S.raw_records.toLocaleString()} records, {S.normalized_lines.toLocaleString()} lines, {S.normalized_brands} brands) is free to download below. Source data is NHTSA's, pulled {UPDATED}; please cite <a href={SOURCE_URL}>NHTSA</a> and this site.</div>
  <div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Format</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead><tbody>{files.map(([f, t, d]) => <tr><td><a href={`/data/${f}`} download>{f}</a></td><td>{t}</td><td>{d}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <h2>CSV columns</h2>
  <div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>id</td><td>NHTSA record id</td></tr><tr><td>brand, brand_slug, brand_raw</td><td>Normalized brand, URL slug, and the brand string exactly as NHTSA filed it</td></tr>
    <tr><td>line, line_slug</td><td>Normalized tire line name and slug</td></tr><tr><td>size_raw</td><td>NHTSA's size text, unchanged</td></tr>
    <tr><td>size_key, size_label, size_type, size_suffix</td><td>Parsed size (e.g. 225-65r17, 225/65R17, P/LT, load/speed text); blank if NHTSA gave no specific size</td></tr>
    <tr><td>treadwear, traction, temperature</td><td>UTQG grades; blank when missing or invalid</td></tr><tr><td>quality_flags</td><td>Notes on invalid or missing source values</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h2>What each file is</h2>
  <p>The record file is the normalized copy of the NHTSA pull: {S.raw_records.toLocaleString()} rows, one per NHTSA record id. The API reported {S.reported_total.toLocaleString()} records and the pull matched that total. Brand spelling in the source is inconsistent. {S.raw_brand_strings} raw brand strings become {S.normalized_brands} brands, and {S.raw_product_names.toLocaleString()} product names become {S.normalized_lines.toLocaleString()} lines. Distinct brands with similar names are not merged. The line file rolls those rows up to one object per line, with the median treadwear, a percentile against other lines, and a rank inside the brand. The size file keeps only records that name a specific size: {S.records_with_explicit_size.toLocaleString()} of {S.raw_records.toLocaleString()} records, covering {S.distinct_explicit_sizes} sizes. The other {S.records_all_sizes_or_range.toLocaleString()} records say “All sizes” or give a range, so they stay on the line and do not appear under one size.</p>
  <h2>What is not in these files</h2>
  <p>{S.records_missing_or_invalid_treadwear} records have a missing or zero treadwear grade and are left out of treadwear statistics. {S.records_with_quality_flags} records carry a quality flag; the raw value is still in the record file. NHTSA’s active flag is false on every row in this pull, and the complaint and recall counts are zero everywhere, so those fields are not used as a status. Prices, vehicle fitment, and mileage warranties are not in the NHTSA ratings file. A warranty figure on a tire-line page, when one is shown, comes from the maker’s own page and is not a column here.</p>
  <p>The median treadwear across lines in this pull is {S.treadwear_overall_median}. Of the {S.distinct_explicit_sizes} named sizes, {S.sizes_with_ge5_lines} have at least five rated lines and {S.sizes_with_ge10_lines} have at least ten. Definitions of treadwear, traction, and temperature, and the cleaning rules, are on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page. Grade rules are in <a href={CFR_URL}>49 CFR 575.104</a> and on <a href={NHTSA_GUIDE}>NHTSA TireWise</a>.</p>
  <p>License note: U.S. federal government works are generally not subject to U.S. copyright (17 U.S.C. §105); see <a href="https://www.usa.gov/government-works">usa.gov/government-works</a>. Our added fields (slugs, parsed sizes, ranks) are provided as-is, with no warranty.</p>
</Base>
